  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass $2 \\mathrm{~kg}$ is moving such that at time $t$, its position, in meter, is given by $\\vec{r}(t)=5 \\hat{i}-2 t^2 \\hat{j}$. The angular momentum of the particle at $t=2 s$ about the origin in $\\mathrm{kg} \\mathrm{m}^{-2} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "l40I2",
      "text": "\n$-80 \\hat{k}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "fi1aK",
      "text": "\n$(10 \\hat{i}-16 \\hat{j})$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XOa94",
      "text": "\n$-40 \\hat{k}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PqNfO",
      "text": "\n$40 \\hat{k}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Angular momentum $\\mathrm{L}=\\mathrm{m}(\\mathrm{v} \\times \\mathrm{r})$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =2 \\mathrm{~kg}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{dr}}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\times \\mathrm{r}\\right)=2 \\mathrm{~kg}\\left(4 \\mathrm{t} \\times \\times 5 \\mathrm{i}-2 \\mathrm{t}^2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}\\right) \\\\\n& =2 \\mathrm{~kg}(-20 \\mathrm{t} \\hat{\\mathrm{k}})=2 \\mathrm{~kg} \\times-20 \\times 2 \\mathrm{~m}^{-2} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1} \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\\\\n& =-80 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
